covert 19 combined with the usual winter  pressures is putting immense pressure on  our hospitals we have seen the number of  coronavirus cases  rising in the past couple of weeks and  that is now feeding through  to the number of people in hospital as  of yesterday there were 20  426 people in hospital in england with  covert 19  and that means they're now more people  in hospital with coronavirus than at any  one point during the first wave back in  april  the number of patients in hospital  peaked at just under 19  000. it dropped off quite substantially  over the summer but it's been rising  again  and that has now passed 20 000. doctors  and paramedics say  that is putting a huge strain on the nhs  but we know  that winter is always a tricky time for  the health service so this  is this just standard winter pressures  or are things worse because of the  coronavirus  this graph shows us the number of  emergency admissions hospitals in  england dating from june 2015 to  november  this year which is the most recent data  that we have and this shows us that  although  there are some fluctuations with numbers  typically rising around the winter  months  the number of emergency admissions is  not higher than its similar points in  the last few years however  this doesn't tell us how long patients  are in hospital for it's worth  remembering  that we don't have december's figure yet  and because there's always a lag of a  couple of weeks from getting infected  to potentially going into hospital the  rise in cases we have seen in the last  fortnight  could push that level up so it's not a  complete picture yet  we've been hearing though from doctors  and nurses who say hospitals are under  real pressure and one of the reasons for  this may be  staffing there are around 84 000 vacant  staff positions in the nhs  38 000 of which are in nursing posts  in fact one in 10 nursing posts in the  nhs  are currently unfilled and that's partly  explained  why even though admissions are not yet  exceeding the levels we've seen in  previous years  on the ground things are still very  stretched
 

